foresee|anticipate-future|VERB|anticipate a future event|To recognize in advance that something may happen.|thấy trước; dự liệu|The organizers foresaw delays and allowed extra time for the journey.|Ban tổ chức dự liệu việc chậm trễ và dành thêm thời gian cho hành trình.|Transitive; foresee something or foresee that; foresaw, foreseen. Foreseeing is anticipation, not certain knowledge of the future.|-
increasingly|more-over-time|ADVERB|more over time|More and more as time passes.|ngày càng|The library became increasingly popular after extending its opening hours.|Thư viện ngày càng được ưa chuộng sau khi kéo dài giờ mở cửa.|Before an adjective or adverb; also before a main verb. Increasingly describes a trend rather than one fixed degree.|0
peninsula|land-mostly-surrounded-by-water|NOUN|land extending into water|A piece of land surrounded by water on most sides but joined to a larger land area.|bán đảo|A narrow road connects the peninsula's villages with the mainland.|Một con đường hẹp nối các làng trên bán đảo với phần đất liền chính.|Countable; a peninsula, peninsulas. A peninsula remains connected to land, unlike an island.|-
stern|serious-and-strict|ADJECTIVE|serious and strict|Serious and firm in expecting people to behave properly.|nghiêm khắc; nghiêm nghị|The coach gave the noisy players a stern look.|Huấn luyện viên nhìn những cầu thủ ồn ào bằng ánh mắt nghiêm nghị.|Stern look or warning; stern with someone. This adjective is distinct from the ship-part noun.|-
wax|meltable-substance|NOUN|solid substance that softens with heat|A substance that is solid at ordinary temperatures and softens or melts when heated, often used for candles or polish.|sáp|The artist warmed the wax before shaping the small model.|Người nghệ sĩ làm ấm sáp trước khi tạo hình cho mô hình nhỏ.|Usually uncountable material noun; a piece of wax. A wax can name a particular type.|-
